    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1028">

                <pb facs="1064" n="1050" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1050"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.24/10–344</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Miss Laura Iredale of the Division of
                        American Republics Analysis and Liaison, for Mr. Henry Dearborn, Division of
                        North and West Coast Affairs</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-10-03">October 3, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In answer to your request for figures on lend-lease materials to Ecuador, I have
                    obtained the following figures from Mr. Willett in FEA.</p>
                <p>The information which he has given me covers total lend-lease exports to Ecuador
                    from March 1941 through July, 1944. The types of exports are divided into the
                    following categories: <table cols="2" rend="width: 99%" rendition="#center"
                        rows="6">
                        <row role="label">
                            <cell rend="padding-left: 3em">Ordnance</cell>
                            <cell role="num">$493,360</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell rend="padding-left: 3em">Aircraft</cell>
                            <cell role="num">1,308,191</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell rend="padding-left: 3em">Tanks and other vehicles</cell>
                            <cell role="num">1,219,989</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell rend="padding-left: 3em">Water craft</cell>
                            <cell role="num">44,000</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell rend="padding-left: 3em">Agriculture</cell>
                            <cell role="num">1,105,000</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell rend="padding-left: 3em">Industry</cell>
                            <cell role="num">1,285,307</cell>
                        </row>
                    </table>
                </p>
                <p>The total figure for lend-lease exports to Ecuador from March, 1941 through July,
                    1944 is $4,351,952.</p>
                <p>I think it will interest you to know that Mr. Willett has offered to prepare a
                    table of lend-lease exports to the other American Republics divided into the
                    categories listed above. He has promised to send them <pb facs="1065" n="1051"
                        xml:id="pg1051"/> to my office on a monthly basis, consequently, current
                    figures on lend-lease should be available in RL files from now on.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
